   $q$In paragraph 5, biologists find the label "indestructible" "dubious." Based on the evidence that follows, "dubious" most nearly means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"exaggerated on purpose so that articles will sell","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"too technical for ordinary readers to understand","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"questionable because the facts do not fully support it","is_correct":true},{"text":"accurate for active tardigrades but not for tuns","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$questionable because the facts do not fully support it$q$, $q$The next sentences give facts that undercut the label: active tardigrades "are fragile" and tuns "eventually perish," so dubious means doubtful or questionable. The text never says why articles use the label, so the idea that it is exaggerated on purpose to sell articles is an unsupported guess.$q$, 'draft', '9e2ee895-e308-57c5-b15f-9300a0d96898')
