   $q$Considering the experiments described earlier, the word "prodigious" in paragraph 6 most nearly means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"unproven and imaginary","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-contrast"},{"text":"harmful to other species","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"remarkably impressive","is_correct":true},{"text":"ordinary and expected","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$remarkably impressive$q$, $q$The abilities include solving a maze and growing a network like rail lines, and they are striking enough to make scientists "reconsider what counts as decision making," so prodigious means remarkably impressive. The doubters question what the abilities mean, not whether they happened, so "unproven and imaginary" misreads the contrast.$q$, 'draft', 'fecbe175-7fa7-5b78-9537-bfdb8012095e')
